  "comments": "<p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/61751c0889728.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/61751c0889728.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>The $2 coin was introduced into circulation in Australia in 1988 to replace the old familiar green $2 note. In 1999 the Ian Rank-Broadley 4th Portrait of Queen Elizabeth II was introduced on the Obverse of the coin. The Reverse was unchanged from prior years.&nbsp;<br><br>This coin was included in the 30th Anniversary of the Two Dollar Coin (1988-2018) Set:<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5b9d3d05e5b9d.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5b9d3d05e5b9d.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5b9d3d19f3ee8.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5b9d3d19f3ee8.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>© Amer Salmeh</p>",
